**Read:** [Safety in Academic Chemistry Laboratories — ACS, eighth edition](../sources/ACS-Academic-Laboratories.lingua#r_1GAGRBYCJGJAY86HQCNE9S66EP), the entire publication; [Química geral no laboratório — Marcela Boroski, organizer](../sources/Quimica-geral-no-laboratorio.lingua#r_48YEN2SA34DW0FPCSTMVTW3CTD), the complete manual as an initial overview; [Prudent Practices in the Laboratory — National Research Council](../sources/Prudent-Practices.lingua#r_3RPEFRP5NBW53ECS7EFQX6D6ZK), planning, hazards, operations, and waste chapters; [Laboratory Safety for Chemistry Students — Hill and Finster, third edition](../sources/ACS-Laboratory-Safety-Textbook.lingua#r_7TD6AG2TZZ0GS0EWJMC8KC9SB0), the relevant introductory sections, then the whole textbook during sustained practical study.

An experiment needs more than a correct equation: suitable equipment and materials, a defined procedure, training, an assessment of its particular hazards and scale, reliable observations, and a way to handle outputs and wastes. Read the complete ACS student booklet and the laboratory manual before selecting a practical activity. Continue into the full safety texts for sustained laboratory and research work.

Use the RAMP process to connect each operation with evidence: recognize hazards from appropriate current information; assess exposure and credible failure conditions; choose controls suited to those risks; and prepare for the actual emergency arrangements of the laboratory. Quantity, concentration, temperature, pressure, energy sources, and compatibility can change an operation's risk even when its reaction equation is familiar.

Distinguish reading, simulation, data analysis, and practical performance. They develop complementary understanding. A calculation can be studied independently; handling chemicals or equipment requires the relevant laboratory conditions and supervision. A virtual success cannot demonstrate accurate pipetting, a secure apparatus, or competence with an unexpected leak or spill.

**Work:** choose an introductory activity from the UNILA manual and write its question, model, measurements, equipment, materials, control arrangements, observations, calculations, limitations, and waste plan. Have a suitably competent supervisor evaluate the actual implementation before laboratory work. If working from published data, state that evidence route and identify which practical skills remain unobserved.

Preserve original observations and explain deviations from a procedure rather than editing them into a more convenient result. Experimental craft and critical interpretation deepen together throughout the later practical programme. These are subject-specific learning demands, not permission requirements for opening or reusing a Record.

**Continue:** [First study — connect identity, amount, observation, and a balance](First-chemical-study.lingua#r_6AD48R8HSNCS1QWP1YGRGDAAVC).

